From a7b9c15deffb3db85dbf616f0956fd1dfbaf858d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:39:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] meson: define feature macros for the aarch64 ops_asmgen tool

ops_asmgen is a native build tool, and add_project_arguments() only
applies to the host machine, so it is compiled with -std=c17 but
without _GNU_SOURCE. glibc then hides strdup(), which the tool uses
through av_strdup(), and GCC rejects the implicit declaration.

Pass the same feature macros as the rest of the project.
---
 libswscale/aarch64/meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libswscale/aarch64/meson.build b/libswscale/aarch64/meson.build
index 4a621ec1b6..c49e301dd2 100644
--- a/libswscale/aarch64/meson.build
+++ b/libswscale/aarch64/meson.build
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ if conf.get('neon', 0) == 1
   ops_asmgen = executable('ops_asmgen',
     files('ops_asmgen.c'),
     include_directories: common_incs,
+    c_args: ['-D_ISOC11_SOURCE', '-D_GNU_SOURCE'],
     native: true,
     install: false
   )
-- 
